cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ertkit in your work, please cite it as below, together with the methods it implements."
title: "ertkit: resistivity inversion for groundwater exploration, with uncertainty and depth of investigation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tiamiyu
    given-names: "Abd'gafar Tunde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1641-7196"
    affiliation: "School of Mathematics, Jilin University"
# A version and a Zenodo DOI are added with release 0.1.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdgafartunde/ertkit"
url: "https://abdgafartunde.github.io/ertkit/"
abstract: >-
  ertkit inverts vertical electrical sounding (VES) data for groundwater
  exploration; 2.5-D electrical resistivity tomography (ERT) follows in later
  releases. Each result comes with a data error model and a fit to the noise
  level, linearized parameter uncertainty, sensitivity and a depth of
  investigation.
keywords:
  - electrical resistivity tomography
  - vertical electrical sounding
  - groundwater
  - inverse problems
  - uncertainty quantification
